                <pb facs="0430" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/121: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-08T12:00:00-00:44">November 8,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 10:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>60. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 45, November 6, 5 p.m. President’s
                    message recommended that slavery convention of 1926 be ratified during the
                    present session.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
